      <!-- ═══ SECTION 2 - Requirements ═══ -->
      <section id="requirements" class="guide-section reveal">
        <p class="section-label">Step 1</p>
        <h2 class="guide-section-title">
          <span class="title-icon"><i class="fas fa-microchip"></i></span>
          System Requirements
        </h2>
        <p class="guide-desc">
          NT:NH is a 1.7.10 modpack. It runs on most hardware - but it benefits from a
          dedicated RAM allocation and a modern JVM. Below are the recommended specs.
        </p>

        <div class="req-bar">
          <div class="req-grid">
            <div class="req-item">
              <span class="req-label">Minecraft Version</span>
              <span class="req-value"><span>1.7.10</span></span>
            </div>
            <div class="req-item">
              <span class="req-label">Java Version</span>
              <span class="req-value">Java <span>8</span> (64-bit)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="req-item">
              <span class="req-label">Recommended RAM</span>
              <span class="req-value"><span>4&ndash;6 GB</span> allocated</span>
            </div>
            <div class="req-item">
              <span class="req-label">Mod Loader</span>
              <span class="req-value"><span>Forge</span> (included)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="req-item">
              <span class="req-label">OS</span>
              <span class="req-value">Windows &middot; macOS &middot; <span>Linux</span></span>
            </div>
            <div class="req-item">
              <span class="req-label">Disk Space</span>
              <span class="req-value">~<span>2 GB</span> free</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="notice notice-warn">
          <i class="fas fa-triangle-exclamation"></i>
          <div class="notice-content">
            <strong>Java 8 Required</strong>
            Minecraft 1.7.10 with Forge requires Java 8 specifically. Java 17 or 21 will not work.
            Make sure your launcher points to a 64-bit Java 8 installation - some launchers bundle their own.
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="divider" style="margin-bottom:3rem;"></div>

      <!-- ═══ SECTION 3 - Install ═══ -->
      <section id="install" class="guide-section reveal">
        <p class="section-label">Step 2</p>
        <h2 class="guide-section-title">
          <span class="title-icon"><i class="fas fa-download"></i></span>
          Download &amp; Install
        </h2>
        <p class="guide-desc">
          Each GitHub release ships four archive formats. Pick the one that matches your launcher,
          or grab the Native archive if you want to manage things yourself.
          Click a tab below to see the step-by-step guide for that method.
        </p>

        <!-- ── Tabs ── -->
        <div class="dl-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Installer methods">
          <button class="dl-tab active" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-tab="prism">
            <i class="fas fa-layer-group"></i> Prism / MMC
            <span class="pill pill-green" style="margin-left:0.25rem;">Recommended</span>
          </button>
          <button class="dl-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="curseforge">
            <i class="fas fa-fire-flame-curved"></i> CurseForge
          </button>
          <button class="dl-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="modrinth">
            <i class="fas fa-leaf"></i> Modrinth
          </button>
          <button class="dl-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="technic">
            <i class="fas fa-wrench"></i> Technic
          </button>
          <button class="dl-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-tab="native">
            <i class="fas fa-folder-open"></i> Native
          </button>
        </div>

        <!-- ── Prism / MMC ── -->
        <div class="method-panel active" id="tab-prism">
          <div class="notice notice-tip">
            <i class="fas fa-circle-check"></i>
            <div class="notice-content">
              <strong>Recommended Method</strong>
              Prism Launcher is free, open-source, and supports all major archive formats including
              MMC/Prism, CurseForge, and Modrinth packs. Use the <strong>MMC_Prism</strong> archive for
              best compatibility. Download Prism at
              <a href="https://prismlauncher.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#4ade80;">prismlauncher.org</a>.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="step-list">
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">1</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Install Prism Launcher</p>
                <p class="step-desc">
                  Download and install <a href="https://prismlauncher.org/download/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Prism Launcher</a>
                  for your operating system (Windows, macOS, Linux). During first launch Prism will ask you to
                  log in to a Microsoft account. A valid, paid Minecraft account is required.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">2</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Download the MMC_Prism Archive</p>
                <p class="step-desc">
                  Head to the <a href="/download">Downloads page</a> and find the latest release.
                  Under <strong>Assets</strong>, download the file ending in <span class="ic">_MMC_Prism.zip</span>.
                  Save it somewhere accessible - your Downloads folder is fine.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">3</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Import into Prism</p>
                <p class="step-desc">
                  Open Prism Launcher. Click <strong>Add Instance</strong> in the top-left toolbar,
                  then select the <strong>Import</strong> tab. Click <strong>Browse</strong>, select
                  the ZIP you just downloaded, then click <strong>OK</strong>. Prism will download all
                  required mods automatically.
                </p>
                <div class="code-note">
                  <i class="fas fa-lightbulb"></i>
                  Prism also accepts CurseForge and Modrinth archives via the same Import dialog -
                  use whichever zip you have. MMC_Prism is always the preferred format.
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">4</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Allocate RAM &amp; Launch</p>
                <p class="step-desc">
                  Right-click the NT:NH instance &rarr; <strong>Edit</strong> &rarr; <strong>Settings</strong> &rarr;
                  <strong>Java</strong>. Set maximum memory to at least <strong>4096 MB</strong> (4 GB),
                  ideally 5&ndash;6 GB. Hit <strong>Launch</strong> and wait for the first load -
                  it takes a minute or two.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ── CurseForge ── -->
        <div class="method-panel" id="tab-curseforge">
          <div class="notice notice-info">
            <i class="fas fa-circle-info"></i>
            <div class="notice-content">
              <strong>CurseForge Launcher Required</strong>
              This method uses the official CurseForge desktop app. Requires a free CurseForge account
              and a valid, paid Minecraft account. Download it at
              <a href="https://www.curseforge.com/download/app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">curseforge.com/download/app</a>.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="step-list">
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">1</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Install CurseForge Launcher</p>
                <p class="step-desc">
                  Download and install the <a href="https://www.curseforge.com/download/app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CurseForge App</a>.
                  Sign in with your CurseForge account and make sure Minecraft is set up under the Games section.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">2</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Download the CurseForge Archive</p>
                <p class="step-desc">
                  Go to the <a href="/download">Downloads page</a>, find the latest release, and download
                  the file ending in <span class="ic">_CurseForge.zip</span>.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">3</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Import via the "Import" Button</p>
                <p class="step-desc">
                  In the CurseForge app, go to <strong>Minecraft &rarr; Create Custom Profile</strong>,
                  then click the <strong>Import</strong> button (it may appear as a folder icon near
                  the top of the My Modpacks section). Select the downloaded ZIP.
                  CurseForge will install all mods automatically.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">4</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Adjust RAM &amp; Play</p>
                <p class="step-desc">
                  Click the three-dot menu on the NT:NH profile &rarr; <strong>Profile Options</strong>.
                  Enable custom memory settings and set at least <strong>4096 MB</strong>. Then click Play.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ── Modrinth ── -->
        <div class="method-panel" id="tab-modrinth">
          <div class="notice notice-info">
            <i class="fas fa-circle-info"></i>
            <div class="notice-content">
              <strong>Modrinth App Required</strong>
              This method uses the Modrinth launcher - free and open-source. Requires a paid Minecraft account.
              Download it at <a href="https://modrinth.com/app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">modrinth.com/app</a>.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="step-list">
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">1</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Install the Modrinth App</p>
                <p class="step-desc">
                  Download the <a href="https://modrinth.com/app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Modrinth App</a>
                  for your platform and sign in with your Microsoft account during setup.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">2</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Download the Modrinth Archive</p>
                <p class="step-desc">
                  Visit the <a href="/download">Downloads page</a> and grab the file ending in
                  <span class="ic">_Modrinth.mrpack</span> from the latest release.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">3</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Import the .mrpack File</p>
                <p class="step-desc">
                  In the Modrinth App, click the <strong>+</strong> button and choose
                  <strong>Import from file</strong>. Select the <span class="ic">.mrpack</span> file.
                  All mods will be downloaded automatically.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">4</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Set RAM &amp; Launch</p>
                <p class="step-desc">
                  Click the NT:NH instance &rarr; <strong>Edit</strong> &rarr; <strong>Java Settings</strong>
                  and allocate at least <strong>4 GB</strong>. Then press <strong>Play</strong>.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ── Technic ── -->
        <div class="method-panel" id="tab-technic">
          <div class="notice notice-info">
            <i class="fas fa-circle-info"></i>
            <div class="notice-content">
              <strong>Technic Launcher Required</strong>
              This method uses the Technic Launcher with the official NT:NH modpack page.
              Requires a paid Minecraft account. Download Technic at
              <a href="https://www.technicpack.net/download" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">technicpack.net/download</a>.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="step-list">
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">1</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Install the Technic Launcher</p>
                <p class="step-desc">
                  Download and install the <a href="https://www.technicpack.net/download" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Technic Launcher</a>
                  for your platform. Sign in with your Minecraft account during setup.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">2</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Open the Modpack Page</p>
                <p class="step-desc">
                  In the Technic Launcher, click <strong>Modpacks</strong> and search for
                  <span class="ic">nuclear-tech-new-horizons</span>, or paste the modpack URL directly:
                </p>
                <div class="code-note" style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--orange);">
                  https://www.technicpack.net/modpack/nuclear-tech-new-horizons
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">3</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Install &amp; Configure RAM</p>
                <p class="step-desc">
                  Click <strong>Install</strong> on the NT:NH page. Once installed, go to
                  <strong>Launcher Options &rarr; Java Settings</strong> and set memory to at least
                  <strong>4096 MB</strong>.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">4</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Play</p>
                <p class="step-desc">
                  Select NT:NH from your modpack list and hit <strong>Play</strong>. The launcher
                  handles all mod downloads automatically.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ── Native ── -->
        <div class="method-panel" id="tab-native">
          <div class="notice notice-warn">
            <i class="fas fa-triangle-exclamation"></i>
            <div class="notice-content">
              <strong>Manual / Pirated Launcher Method</strong>
              The Native archive is a raw dump of all modpack files with no launcher structure.
              This method works with any launcher - including KLauncher, TLauncher, and Legacy Launcher -
              since you copy files directly into your <span class="ic">.minecraft</span> folder.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="step-list">
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">1</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Download the Native Archive</p>
                <p class="step-desc">
                  Go to the <a href="/download">Downloads page</a> and download the file ending in
                  <span class="ic">_Native.zip</span> from the latest release.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">2</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Locate Your .minecraft Folder</p>
                <p class="step-desc">Open your launcher and find the game directory, or navigate manually:</p>
                <div class="code-note" style="flex-direction:column;gap:0.35rem;">
                  <div><i class="fab fa-windows" style="color:#60a5fa;"></i>&nbsp;&nbsp;Windows:
                    <span style="color:var(--yellow);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;">%APPDATA%\.minecraft</span>
                  </div>
                  <div><i class="fab fa-apple" style="color:#aaa;"></i>&nbsp;&nbsp;macOS:
                    <span style="color:var(--yellow);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;">~/Library/Application Support/minecraft</span>
                  </div>
                  <div><i class="fab fa-linux" style="color:#4ade80;"></i>&nbsp;&nbsp;Linux:
                    <span style="color:var(--yellow);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;">~/.minecraft</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p class="step-desc" style="margin-top:0.5rem;">
                  If your launcher manages multiple instances, use <em>that</em> instance's game directory
                  instead of the default one.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">3</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Extract and Copy All Files</p>
                <p class="step-desc">
                  Open the Native ZIP and copy <strong>all files and folders</strong> directly into your
                  <span class="ic">.minecraft</span> folder, merging with any existing content.
                  You should end up with a <span class="ic">mods/</span> folder,
                  <span class="ic">config/</span> folder, etc. inside <span class="ic">.minecraft</span>.
                </p>
                <div class="code-note">
                  <i class="fas fa-circle-exclamation"></i>
                  <div class="code-note-text">
                    Do <strong>not</strong> put everything inside a subfolder. The contents of the ZIP go <em>directly</em> into
                    <span style="color:var(--yellow);font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;">.minecraft</span>, not into a nested folder inside it.
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
              <div class="step-num">4</div>
              <div class="step-body">
                <p class="step-title">Install Forge &amp; Launch</p>
                <p class="step-desc">
                  Make sure your launcher is set to use the correct Forge version for 1.7.10
                  (the release notes on GitHub list the exact Forge build required). Allocate at least
                  <strong>4 GB RAM</strong> in your launcher's JVM arguments, then start the game.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="divider" style="margin-bottom:3rem;"></div>

      <!-- ═══ SECTION 4 - Launcher Comparison ═══ -->
      <section id="launchers" class="guide-section reveal">
        <p class="section-label">Reference</p>
        <h2 class="guide-section-title">
          <span class="title-icon"><i class="fas fa-table"></i></span>
          Launcher Comparison
        </h2>
        <p class="guide-desc">
          Quick reference for which archive format to use with which launcher, and which launchers
          require a paid Minecraft account.
        </p>

        <div class="method-table-wrap">
          <table class="method-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Launcher</th>
                <th>Archive to Use</th>
                <th>Paid Account?</th>
                <th>Notes</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Prism Launcher</td>
                <td>
                  <span class="pill pill-green">MMC_Prism</span>
                  <span class="pill pill-orange">CurseForge</span>
                  <span class="pill pill-purple">Modrinth</span>
                </td>
                <td><span class="pill pill-amber">Required</span></td>
                <td style="font-size:0.8rem;">Open-source. Supports all three import formats. MMC_Prism preferred.
                  Does <strong style="color:var(--text-bright);">not</strong> support Native.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>MultiMC</td>
                <td><span class="pill pill-green">MMC_Prism</span></td>
                <td><span class="pill pill-amber">Required</span></td>
                <td style="font-size:0.8rem;">Prism is a fork of MMC. Both support the same archive format.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>CurseForge App</td>
                <td><span class="pill pill-orange">CurseForge</span></td>
                <td><span class="pill pill-amber">Required</span></td>
                <td style="font-size:0.8rem;">Import via the Import button on the My Modpacks page.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Modrinth App</td>
                <td><span class="pill pill-purple">Modrinth</span></td>
                <td><span class="pill pill-amber">Required</span></td>
                <td style="font-size:0.8rem;">Import the .mrpack file via the + button.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Technic Launcher</td>
                <td><span class="pill pill-green">Technic</span></td>
                <td><span class="pill pill-amber">Required</span></td>
                <td style="font-size:0.8rem;">Install directly from the <a href="https://www.technicpack.net/modpack/nuclear-tech-new-horizons" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:var(--orange);">NT:NH Technic page</a>. No archive download needed.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>KLauncher / TLauncher / Legacy Launcher</td>
                <td><span class="pill pill-blue">Native</span></td>
                <td><span class="pill pill-green">Not Required</span></td>
                <td style="font-size:0.8rem;">Extract the Native ZIP into your .minecraft directory manually.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Any other launcher</td>
                <td><span class="pill pill-blue">Native</span></td>
                <td style="font-size:0.8rem;color:var(--text-muted);">Varies</td>
                <td style="font-size:0.8rem;">The Native method works universally for any launcher not listed here.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <div class="notice notice-tip">
          <i class="fas fa-star"></i>
          <div class="notice-content">
            <strong>Why Prism Launcher?</strong>
            Prism is free, open-source, and runs on Windows, macOS, and Linux. It bundles its own Java,
            handles RAM settings per-instance, and can import CurseForge, MMC/Prism, and Modrinth archives.
            If you don't have a preference,
            <a href="https://prismlauncher.org/download/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#4ade80;">start here</a>.
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="divider" style="margin-bottom:3rem;"></div>

      <!-- ═══ SECTION 5 - FAQ ═══ -->
      <section id="faq" class="guide-section reveal">
        <p class="section-label">Help</p>
        <h2 class="guide-section-title">
          <span class="title-icon"><i class="fas fa-circle-question"></i></span>
          Frequently Asked Questions
        </h2>

        <div class="faq-list">

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
              <span class="faq-question-text">The game crashes immediately on launch. What do I do?</span>
              <i class="fas fa-chevron-down faq-chevron"></i>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">
                The most common causes are wrong Java version (must be Java 8 64-bit) or not enough RAM allocated.
                Confirm in your launcher's settings that Java 8 is selected, and that maximum memory is at least
                4096 MB. If the crash persists, open the crash report (in <span class="ic">.minecraft/crash-reports/</span>)
                and paste it in the <a href="https://discord.gg/wtNVzeE5QB" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">#support</a>
                channel on Discord.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
              <span class="faq-question-text">Can I play on a pirated / cracked Minecraft account?</span>
              <i class="fas fa-chevron-down faq-chevron"></i>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">
                The modpack itself works with unofficial launchers (KLauncher, TLauncher, Legacy Launcher).
                Use the <strong>Native</strong> archive and follow the manual installation steps above.
                Note that our official multiplayer server requires a legitimate account to connect.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
              <span class="faq-question-text">How do I update to a new version of NT:NH?</span>
              <i class="fas fa-chevron-down faq-chevron"></i>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">
                If you're using CurseForge, MultiMC, Modrinth, or Prism Launcher, you can use their built-in update feature, which keeps your worlds and settings intact while updating the modpack. For unofficial launchers, you'll need to delete the old folders from the Native.zip archive and replace them with the new ones, as mods are frequently added or removed.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
              <span class="faq-question-text">How much RAM should I allocate?</span>
              <i class="fas fa-chevron-down faq-chevron"></i>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">
                4 GB (4096 MB) is the minimum. 5&ndash;6 GB is ideal for smooth gameplay. More than 8 GB is generally
                counterproductive for 1.7.10 and can cause longer garbage-collection pauses. If you have
                16 GB of system RAM, allocating 5&ndash;6 GB to Minecraft is a sensible target.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
              <span class="faq-question-text">Which archive format should I use with Prism Launcher?</span>
              <i class="fas fa-chevron-down faq-chevron"></i>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">
                Always prefer the <strong>MMC_Prism</strong> archive when using Prism Launcher or MultiMC -
                it's the native format and the most reliable. Prism also accepts CurseForge and Modrinth archives
                if that's what you have. The <strong>Native</strong> archive cannot be imported into Prism -
                it is a raw file dump intended for manual installation only.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
              <span class="faq-question-text">How do I join the multiplayer server?</span>
              <i class="fas fa-chevron-down faq-chevron"></i>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">
                The game includes a default list of multiplayer servers. For unofficial community servers not listed by default, check the official Discord server where they are posted.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="faq-item">
            <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">
              <span class="faq-question-text">I found a bug. Where do I report it?</span>
              <i class="fas fa-chevron-down faq-chevron"></i>
            </button>
            <div class="faq-answer">
              <div class="faq-answer-inner">
                Use the <a href="https://github.com/NTNewHorizons/NTNH/issues/new/choose" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Issues page</a>
                and pick the appropriate template. Include your NT:NH version, a description of the bug,
                steps to reproduce it, and any relevant crash reports or logs. You can also ask in
                <a href="https://discord.gg/wtNVzeE5QB" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Discord</a>
                first to confirm it's a known issue.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ═══ CTA ═══ -->
